# Pull Request: Persist sort field and order when updating a saved view (#457)

## Summary
Resolves #457.
Fixes an issue where updating an existing saved view after modifying document sorting did not persist the updated sort field or sort order to the server.

## Root Cause
In `SavedViewsWidget` (`lib/features/documents/view/widgets/saved_views/saved_views_widget.dart`), when the user clicked "Save changes", `selectedView!.copyWith(...)` updated only `filterRules`. It did not pass `sortField` or `sortReverse` from `widget.filter`. Consequently, `newView.toRequest()` preserved the stale/initial sorting values, sending them to the backend in the update request.

## Changes
- In `SavedViewsWidget`: Added `sortField: widget.filter.sortField?.value` and `sortReverse: widget.filter.sortOrder == SortOrder.descending` to `selectedView!.copyWith(...)` when updating a view.
- Added unit tests in `test/src/features/documents/saved_view_sort_test.dart` to verify that `sortField` and `sortReverse` are properly updated and transmitted via `toRequest()`.

